{"availability":"available","full":"sdiehl/prism","name":"prism","description":"A functional language with algebraic effects, multishot continuations, and native codegen","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":170,"forks":9,"created":"2026-06-20T08:17:48Z","updated":"2026-10-06T10:56:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sdiehl.github.io/prism/","topics":[],"demo":"https://sdiehl.github.io/prism/play/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.205Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.205Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.205Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.205Z","stars":170,"forks":9}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small functional language with algebraic effects, multishot continuations, and native codegen.","Prism is an impure functional programming language whose type system tracks side effects. Effect sets are inferred, extensible rows that compose through ordinary calls instead of monads, and they track observability rather than implementation: an effect handled inside a function vanishes from its type, so internally effectful code can still be analyzed, optimized, and reused as pure code. The language also has rank-N polymorphism, typeclasses, derived lenses and optic paths, fusing streams, deterministic reference counting, and native codegen through LLVM, with an optional textual MLIR…","The compiler is built around deterministic simulation testing at the language level. Prism programs elaborate to a strict A-normal-form call-by-push-value core, definitions and packages are content-addressed by hash, project builds can explain their lineage, and suspended continuations carry the code identity they may resume against. The compiler also builds to WebAssembly, so the playground and gallery run in the browser. The interpreter is a CEK machine modeled in Lean, and it is the differential oracle every native backend must match byte-for-byte."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sdiehl/prism/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f6ab01669fb984094539abad7874347d065a0b7184b11b248cefdf6f908ab472","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.566Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.566Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A small functional language with algebraic effects, multishot continuations, and native codegen.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sdiehl/prism/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f6ab01669fb984094539abad7874347d065a0b7184b11b248cefdf6f908ab472","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sdiehl/prism/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.566Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T10:56:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sdiehl/prism/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:57.567Z","hash":"f6ab01669fb984094539abad7874347d065a0b7184b11b248cefdf6f908ab472","originalBytes":5064,"storedBytes":5064,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["prism","install","llvm","shell","program.pr","native","project","sudo","brew","curl","language","run","check","macos","nix","package","prefix","sdiehl","type","bin","build","cargo","clang","codegen","compiler","debian","fssl","license","needs","path","source","target","ubuntu","apt","backend","bash","binary","builds","code","compile","continuations","core","deterministic","directory","docker","dump","effect","enclosing","every","examples","file","flo","functional","git","github","instead","lib","linux","llvm-22","one","phase","playground","release","sys","they","through","under","usr","a-normal-form","aarch64","above","advanced","after","against.","algebraic","amd64.deb","analyzed","apple","apt.llvm.org","arch","around","available","blog","browser","browser.","built","byte-for-byte.","call-by-push-value","calls","carry","cek","checking.","checksums","clang-22","clean","code.","codegen.","compiling","compose","contains","content-addressed","counti